 (superseded-record . "#hasheq((base-commit . \"64e16a876c603c6e45baafbf4fa1c39b4dc1c261\") (branch . \"main\") (campaign . \"v1.00.24-test-design-hotspot-remediation\") (kind . \"wave-evidence\") (note . \"grouped-mode equivalence characterization and explicit fallback telemetry delivered before any v1.00.27 expansion. The grouped worker and reporter now emit additive per-file evidence fields — requested_execution_mode, effective_execution_mode, and a stable named fallback_reason (string or null) — alongside the existing path/verdict/counts/output fields; old JSON evidence without the new fields continues to parse (tolerant readers, missing fields render as absent/null), and grouped eligibility is unchanged. Every fallback is named with one of a fixed vocabulary: missing-module-plus-test-form, zero-parsed-output, declared-mutation, declared-process-isolation, declared-timeout, declared-global-mutation, unsafe-classified; a grouped request that ends in subprocess execution is always labeled with the exact reason and is counted under subprocess, never grouped. A new fixture matrix tests/fixtures/grouped-mode/ (12 hermetic one-file fixtures) characterizes the required cases: eligible module+ test (eligible-a/b), missing module+ test, top-level-only test body, declared mutation, process isolation, undeclared env mutation, explicit exit, timeout, uncaught exception, stdout/stderr emission, and two eligible files run sequentially in one grouped worker (pair order/cleanup proof). tests/test-runner-grouped-characterization.rkt runs the same matrix in subprocess and grouped modes and asserts verdict+exit-code parity (wall clock may differ, verdicts may not), determinism across repeats, stable fallback names, additive-schema compatibility against a pre-W7 old-shape record, truthful grouped/subprocess counters, and cleanup restoration (CWD, env, parameters, custodian-owned threads/ports per the existing runner contract) with no process-global leakage. Parity findings: 12/12 fixtures verdict-and-exit equivalent; parsed-counts differ only for the uncaught-exception fixture (subprocess parses its 1 failing rackunit check, the grouped worker records the file-level exception and 0 parsed checks) — recorded explicitly in the artifact as a known counts-semantics difference at the exception boundary, with the failed verdict itself preserved. The characterization artifact artifacts/test-runtime/v1.00.24-grouped/characterization.json classifies every fixture eligible/unsafe/fallback with both runs attached (grouped effective mode 6/12, six named fallbacks) plus a repeated-stability block, and is pinned by SHA256SUMS. docs/reports/TEST-GROUPED-MODE-CHARACTERIZATION-v1.00.24.md names the exact future v1.00.27 migration boundary (the 6 currently-effective grouped fixtures and the pair case; everything with a declared/undeclared mutation, isolation, exit, or zero-parse reason stays out) and records that no production test file was re-tiered, no default changed (auto remains unit-fast-only, fast remains subprocess), and no queue activated. Ledger row GROUPED-MODE-CHARACTERIZATION (W7) owns the characterization behavior in fast tier; ownership map updated for the fixture matrix only. Previous-attempt failure (no characterization report, no SHA256SUMS, and no wave-evidence/review/validation records delivered, with a parity definition that wrongly compared parsed counts) is addressed: this attempt delivers all three records, the report, the pinned artifact, and a verdict-level parity definition with counts differences explicit. Focused gates at HEAD: test-run-tests-in-process-mode, test-run-tests-reporting-truthfulness, test-runner-grouped-characterization, inventory --unit-fast-audit, inventory --gate-ownership-map --check all exit 0; the two suite executions in the declared verify chain (--suite unit-fast --mode grouped --json-out and --suite fast) are executed by the coordinator-owned verification lane.\") (records . (#hasheq((owner . \"q-agent\") (state . \"implemented\") (tests . (\"scripts/run-tests/runner.rkt\" \"scripts/run-tests/reporting.rkt\")) (wp . \"W7.1\")) #hasheq((owner . \"q-agent\") (state . \"implemented\") (tests . (\"tests/fixtures/grouped-mode/\" \"tests/test-runner-grouped-characterization.rkt\")) (wp . \"W7.2\")) #hasheq((owner . \"q-agent\") (state . \"implemented\") (tests . (\"scripts/run-tests/inventory.rkt\" \"docs/reports/TEST-GATE-OWNERSHIP-v1.00.24.json\" \"docs/reports/TEST-GATE-OWNERSHIP-v1.00.24.md\")) (wp . \"W7.3\")) #hasheq((owner . \"q-agent\") (state . \"implemented\") (tests . (\"artifacts/test-runtime/v1.00.24-grouped/characterization.json\" \"artifacts/test-runtime/v1.00.24-grouped/SHA256SUMS\" \"docs/reports/TEST-GROUPED-MODE-CHARACTERIZATION-v1.00.24.md\" \"docs/reports/TEST-RETIER-LEDGER-v1.00.24.rktd\")) (wp . \"W7.4\")) #hasheq((owner . \"q-agent\") (state . \"implemented\") (tests . (\"docs/reports/gsd-wave-evidence/v1.00.24-w7.rktd\" \"docs/reports/gsd-wave-reviews/v1.00.24-w7.rktd\" \"docs/reports/gsd-wave-validation/v1.00.24-w7.rktd\")) (wp . \"W7.5\")))) (status . \"completed\") (wave . \"W7\"))")
